;; spec:   stdlib §2.3 (Reducible: nth traps out of range), §1.2 P5; plan §6 L5a (RangeLen is the element type's contract)
;; expect: trap
;; trap:   nth: index out of range
;; roots:  ../../lib support
;; range-nth, the method a Range's nth is built on, traps on its own for an index outside the range, so that a
;; user number type that implements RangeLen and a caller that skips nth's own check get the same answer
;; (nth has checked a negative index before it calls). The float walk would otherwise return the start.
(ns main (:use fib.core fib.seq))

(defun main () -> i64
  (if (= (range-nth 0.0 1.0 0.25 -1) 0.0) 1 0))
